/*
RMSTEST_27 - what does a NEGATIVE circle_radius do
preview-design.md Sec.6.1, and the open half of the radiusPercent min decision

QUESTION
guide:842 documents %Radius as a number in the range 1-50. guide:844 adds that
"0 will disable circle_radius", which Tests 2 and 5 confirmed means the
attribute behaves exactly as if absent. Nothing anywhere addresses a NEGATIVE
value, and RMSTEST_2 and RMSTEST_5 only ever tested 0.

This is not idle. language.json declares radiusPercent with min 1, so RMS0203
currently false-warns on the legal circle_radius 0. The fix is a one-line data
change, but "widen the min to 0" and "widen the min to allow negatives" are
different changes and we cannot pick between them without knowing whether a
negative is legal RMS or an author error worth warning about.

Precedent says do not assume a negative is simply rejected. Negative
base_elevation resolves to 16 (RMSTEST_4), and negative border values are
explicitly legal (guide:887). RMS tolerates negatives in more places than the
guide's stated ranges suggest.

METHOD
Byte-for-byte RMSTEST_24 with one line added: circle_radius -20. Everything
else - SNOW base, eight player lands, tile budget, clumping, fuzziness - is
identical, so RMSTEST_24's measured result IS the control and no new control
run is needed.

Base terrain is SNOW rather than WATER for the reason RMSTEST_24 gives: an
island layout would make DE auto-paint a BEACH ring at every land/water
boundary, which shifts patch edges and is the trap that made the first attempt
at item 7c unreadable.

GENERATE AT TINY (120) WITH 8 PLAYERS. Same as RMSTEST_24, because the
comparison is only valid against a control at the same size and player count.

THE FOUR CANDIDATE READINGS, and each has its own signature
  (a) Treated like 0, i.e. as if the attribute were absent.
      mean distance from center ~50 tiles, sd ~7
  (b) Absolute value taken, so radius 20 percent of full width.
      mean ~24 tiles, and sd ~0
  (c) Clamped to the declared minimum of 1, so radius 1 percent.
      mean ~1.2 tiles, all eight lands piled on the center
  (d) Taken literally as a negative radius.
      Expect nonsense: everything at center, or a failed generation

PREDICTIONS, RECORDED BEFORE THE RUN
1. (a). A negative is most likely folded into the same "not a usable radius"
   branch that 0 already takes. Recorded as the prediction precisely because it
   is the convenient answer - it would let radiusPercent's min go to 0 and treat
   anything below as the same disable sentinel.
2. TWO readings separate these, not one, and the second is the one to trust.
   The MEAN distance separates (a) from (b) from (c). But the SPREAD separates
   (a) from (b) independently: an explicit circle_radius carries variance 0 by
   default (guide:847), so reading (b) predicts a PERFECT ring with all eight
   radii equal, while reading (a) inherits the no-attribute jitter that
   RMSTEST_24 measured at sd 7.11. Two independent signals agreeing is what
   makes this one run sufficient.
3. Eight GRASS patches. Fewer means lands merged and those centroids are not
   origins - see RMSTEST_25's note on merged patches.

RUN IT FIVE TIMES. Eight origins is a small sample for a spread, and the ring
rotation differs per run. Five runs gives 40 radii, matching RMSTEST_24's
sample exactly so the two are directly comparable.

READ IT WITH
  python probe_scenario.py "<scenario>" --patches GRASS
  Map center on a 120 map is 59.5, 59.5. Distance from center is
  sqrt((cx-59.5)^2 + (cy-59.5)^2) on the printed centroids.
  Compare mean AND sd against RMSTEST_24's 50.44 and 7.11.

IF THE ANSWER IS (b), ONE FOLLOW-UP IS WANTED
Absolute-value handling raises the question of what happens above the
documented 50. Re-run this script with circle_radius -60: if the mean lands at
60 percent of width the value is passed through unclamped, and guide:846's
warning about values over 50 forcing players into the corners applies to
negatives too.
*/

<PLAYER_SETUP>
  random_placement

<LAND_GENERATION>
  base_terrain SNOW

  create_player_lands
  {
    terrain_type GRASS
    number_of_tiles 60
    base_size 3
    clumping_factor 20
    border_fuzziness 0
    circle_radius -20
  }

<ELEVATION_GENERATION>


<TERRAIN_GENERATION>

<OBJECTS_GENERATION>

<CONNECTION_GENERATION>
